      "writtenOn": "2022-09-07T10:52:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hi Michael/Nikita,\nThe proposed Java @systemApi for Virtualization is contained in this CL - see the files under javalib/; VirtualMachineManager is the top level class.\nThe actual changes here are in a sense unimportant - I\u0027m adding @SystemApi to the existing private platform API, with changes to keep API lint happy and to ensure our tests etc build against the API stubs.\nBut I would be very interested in your thoughts on the API itself.",
      "revId": "8e1dddb0b98fb9d6ce36673f0c180dbb86286319",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "afc15d1e_d8a93b91",
        "filename": "javalib/src/android/system/virtualmachine/VirtualMachine.java",
        "patchSetId": 9
      },
      "lineNbr": 137,
      "author": {
        "id": 1006497
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-09-07T12:10:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Is died STATUS_STOPPED or STATUS_DELETED? Ideally we\u0027d use the same terms in both the callback and here for the status of the VM.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 132,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 137,
        "endChar": 0
      },
      "revId": "8e1dddb0b98fb9d6ce36673f0c180dbb86286319",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "bac2e822_a77a2dc5",
        "filename": "javalib/src/android/system/virtualmachine/VirtualMachine.java",
        "patchSetId": 9
      },
      "lineNbr": 137,
      "author": {
        "id": 1060831
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-09-08T10:55:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "They both exist and are different.\n\nWhen a virtual machine is created is it in STATUS_STOPPED (I added that to the create() documentation).\nFrom there it can transition to STATUS_RUNNING and back to STATUS_STOPPED.\nOnce it moves to STATUS_DELETED that\u0027s the end; you can then re-create, at which point you get a new VirtualMachine in STATUS_STOPPED.\n\nThe callbacks are all about what happens to the VM after the stopped -\u003e running transition.\n\nI guess the most obvious inconsistency is that the callback onDied() should probably be called onStopped(). And we should perhaps have a different and less morbid name for @DeathReason. (Which is easy enough at the Java level; changing it at the lower levels would be a rather massive refactoring.)\n\nThere isn\u0027t a callback for stopped -\u003e deleted because it only happens when delete() is called, rather than spontaneously.",
      "parentUuid": "afc15d1e_d8a93b91",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 132,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 137,
        "endChar": 0
      },
      "revId": "8e1dddb0b98fb9d6ce36673f0c180dbb86286319",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
